#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "As of %s %s, the you can control how often %s flushes transactions to disk.  The default is 1 second, but in high I/O systems setting to a value greater than 1 can allow disk I/O to be more sequential"
msgstr "Site na %s %s, ị nwere ike ịchịkwa ugboro ole %s na-ebunye azụmahịa na diski. Ndabere bụ sekọnd 1, mana na sistemụ I/O dị elu ịtọ ka ọ bụrụ uru karịrị 1 nwere ike inye ohere ka diski I/O dịkwuo n'usoro"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Okwu"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Current Value"
msgstr "Ọnụọgụ Ugbu a"

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "Depending on the number of logins and use of spine data collector, %s will need many connections.  The calculation for spine is: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), then you must leave headroom for user connections, which will change depending on the number of concurrent login accounts."
msgstr "Dabere na ọnụọgụ nbanye na iji ngwa nchịkọta data spine, %s ga-achọ ọtụtụ njikọ. Mgbakọ maka spine bụ: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), mgbe ahụ ị ga-ahapụ ohere maka njikọ onye ọrụ, nke ga-agbanwe dabere na ọnụọgụ akaụntụ nbanye dị n'otu oge."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "If using the Kadupul Performance Booster and choosing a memory storage engine, you have to be careful to flush your Performance Booster buffer before the system runs out of memory table space.  This is done two ways, first reducing the size of your output column to just the right size.  This column is in the tables poller_output, and poller_output_boost.  The second thing you can do is allocate more memory to memory tables.  We have arbitrarily chosen a recommended value of 10%% of system memory, but if you are using SSD disk drives, or have a smaller system, you may ignore this recommendation or choose a different storage engine.  You may see the expected consumption of the Performance Booster tables under Console -> System Utilities -> View Boost Status."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji Kadupul Performance Booster ma na-ahọrọ injin nchekwa ebe nchekwa, ị ga-akpachara anya kpochapụ buffer Performance Booster gị tupu ohere tebụl ebe nchekwa agwụ na sistemụ. A na-eme nke a n'ụzọ abụọ, nke mbụ belata ogo kọlụm mmepụta gị ruo n'ogo kwesịrị ekwesị. Kọlụm a dị na tebụl poller_output, na poller_output_boost. Ihe nke abụọ ị nwere ike ime bụ ikenye ebe nchekwa karịa na tebụl ebe nchekwa. Anyị họọrọ uru akwadoro nke 10%% nke ebe nchekwa sistemụ n'ụzọ nkịtị, mana ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji diski SSD, ma ọ bụ nwee sistemụ pere mpe, ị nwere ike ileghara ntụziaka a anya ma ọ bụ họrọ injin nchekwa dị iche. Ị nwere ike ịhụ oriri a tụrụ anya ya nke tebụl Performance Booster n'okpuru Console -> Ngwaọrụ Sistemụ -> Lee Ọnọdụ Boost."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 200 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 100000 can be used."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na ị nwere diski SSD, jiri atụmatụ a. Ọ bụrụ na ị nwere diski ike anụ ahụ, jiri 200 * ọnụọgụgụ diski na-arụ ọrụ na nhazi. Ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji NVMe ma ọ bụ PCIe Flash, enwere ike iji ọnụọgụgụ buru ibu karịa ruo 100000."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 2000 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 200000 can be used."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na ị nwere diski SSD, jiri atụmatụ a. Ọ bụrụ na ị nwere diski ike anụ ahụ, jiri 2000 * ọnụọgụgụ diski na-arụ ọrụ na nhazi. Ọ bụrụ na ị na-eji NVMe ma ọ bụ PCIe Flash, enwere ike iji ọnụọgụgụ buru ibu karịa ruo 200000."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion. Otherwise, do not set this setting."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na ị nwere diski SSD, jiri atụmatụ a. Ma ọ bụghị ya, etinyela ntọala a."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If your tables have very large indexes, you must operate with the Barracuda innodb_file_format and the innodb_large_prefix equal to 1.  Failure to do this may result in plugins that can not properly create tables."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na tebụl gị nwere ndeksi buru ibu nke ukwuu, ị ga-arụ ọrụ na Barracuda innodb_file_format na innodb_large_prefix hà ka 1. Ịghara ime nke a nwere ike ime ka plugins ghara ịmepụta tebụl nke ọma."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "InnoDB will hold as much tables and indexes in system memory as is possible.  Therefore, you should make the innodb_buffer_pool large enough to hold as much of the tables and index in memory.  Checking the size of the /var/lib/mysql/cacti directory will help in determining this value.  We are recommending 25%% of your systems total memory, but your requirements will vary depending on your systems size."
msgstr "InnoDB ga-ejide ọtụtụ tebụl na ndeksi na ebe nchekwa sistemụ dịka o kwere mee. Ya mere, ị kwesịrị ime ka innodb_buffer_pool buo ibu zuru oke ijide ọtụtụ tebụl na ndeksi na ebe nchekwa. Ịlele ogo ndekọ /var/lib/mysql/cacti ga-enyere aka ikpebi uru a. Anyị na-atụ aro 25%% nke mkpokọta ebe nchekwa sistemụ gị, mana ihe ị chọrọ ga-adịgasị iche dabere na ogo sistemụ gị."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "It is STRONGLY recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.5.3."
msgstr "A na-atụ aro NKE UKWUU ka ị gbanye InnoDB na ụdị %s ọ bụla karịrị 5.5.3."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "It is recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.1."
msgstr "A na-atụ aro ka ị gbanye InnoDB na ụdị %s ọ bụla karịrị 5.1."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Keeping the table cache larger means less file open/close operations when using innodb_file_per_table."
msgstr "Idebe cache tebụl buru ibu pụtara obere ọrụ imeghe/imechi faịlụ mgbe a na-eji innodb_file_per_table."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Maximum I/O performance happens when you use the O_DIRECT method to flush pages."
msgstr "Arụmọrụ I/O kachasị na-eme mgbe ị na-eji ụzọ O_DIRECT kpochapụ ibe."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "MySQL 5.6+ and MariaDB 10.0+ are great releases, and are very good versions to choose. Make sure you run the very latest release though which fixes a long standing low level networking issue that was causing spine many issues with reliability."
msgstr "MySQL 5.6+ na MariaDB 10.0+ bụ mbipụta magburu onwe ha, ma bụrụ ụdị dị mma ịhọrọ. Jide n'aka na ị na-agba mbipụta kachasị ọhụrụ nke na-edozi nsogbu netwọkụ dị ala nke dịrịla ogologo oge nke na-eme ka spine nwee ọtụtụ nsogbu na ntụkwasị obi."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Note: Many changes below require a database restart"
msgstr "Rịba ama: Ọtụtụ mgbanwe dị n'okpuru chọrọ ịmalitegharị nchekwa data"

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "PHP %s is the minimum version"
msgstr "PHP %s bụ ụdị opekempe"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Recommended Value"
msgstr "Uru Akwadoro"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Rogue queries should not for the database to go offline to others.  Kill these queries before they kill your system."
msgstr "Ajụjụ rogue ekwesịghị ime ka nchekwa data pụọ n'ịntanetị maka ndị ọzọ. Gbuo ajụjụ ndị a tupu ha egbuo sistemụ gị."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "Setting this value to 2 means that you will flush all transactions every second rather than at commit.  This allows %s to perform writing less often."
msgstr "Ịtọ ọnụọgụ a na 2 pụtara na ị ga-ekpochapụ azụmahịa niile kwa sekọnd kama na commit. Nke a na-enye %s ohere ide ihe obere oge."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "This is where metadata is stored. If you had a lot of tables, it would be useful to increase this."
msgstr "Nke a bụ ebe a na-echekwa metadata. Ọ bụrụ na ị nwere ọtụtụ tebụl, ọ ga-aba uru ịba ụba nke a."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "This settings should remain ON unless your Kadupul instances is running on either ZFS or FusionI/O which both have internal journaling to accommodate abrupt system crashes.  However, if you have very good power, and your systems rarely go down and you have backups, turning this setting to OFF can net you almost a 50% increase in database performance."
msgstr "Ntọala a kwesịrị ịnọgide na ON belụsọ ma ọ bụrụ na Kadupul gị na-agba na ZFS ma ọ bụ FusionI/O nke abụọ ha nwere journaling dị n'ime iji nabata ọdịda sistemụ mberede. Agbanyeghị, ọ bụrụ na ị nwere ezigbo ọkụ, na sistemụ gị anaghị ada ada ma ị nwere ndabere, ịgbanwu ntọala a na OFF nwere ike inye gị ihe fọrọ nke nta ka ọ bụrụ 50% mmụba na arụmọrụ database."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Variable"
msgstr "Mgbanwe (Variable)"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When executing subqueries, having a larger temporary table size, keep those temporary tables in memory."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-agba subqueries, inwe nha tebụl nwa oge buru ibu, na-edobe tebụl nwa oge ndị ahụ n'ebe nchekwa."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When performing joins, if they are below this size, they will be kept in memory and never written to a temporary file.  As this is a per connection memory allocation, care must be taken not to increase it too high.  The sum of the join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + Core MySQL/MariaDB memory should be below 80%.  If the recommendation is negative, you must decrease this and or the sort_buffer_size until the recommendation fits within the allowable memory."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eme joins, ọ bụrụ na ha dị n'okpuru nha a, a ga-edobe ha n'ebe nchekwa ma agaghị ede ha na faịlụ nwa oge. Ebe ọ bụ na nke a bụ oke ebe nchekwa maka njikọ ọ bụla, a ga-akpachara anya ka a ghara ịba ụba ya nke ukwuu. Ngụkọta nke join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + ebe nchekwa MySQL/MariaDB isi kwesịrị ịdị n'okpuru 80%. Ọ bụrụ na ndụmọdụ ahụ bụ negative, ị ga-ebelatarịrị nke a na/ma ọ bụ sort_buffer_size ruo mgbe ndụmọdụ ahụ dabara n'ime ebe nchekwa ekwere."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "When using InnoDB storage it is important to keep your table spaces separate.  This makes managing the tables simpler for long time users of %s.  If you are running with this currently off, you can migrate to the per file storage by enabling the feature, and then running an alter statement on all InnoDB tables."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji nchekwa InnoDB ọ dị mkpa idobe oghere tebụl gị iche. Nke a na-eme ka ijikwa tebụl dị mfe maka ndị ọrụ ogologo oge nke %s. Ọ bụrụ na ị na-agba ọsọ na nke a gbanyụrụ ugbu a, ị nwere ike ịkwaga na nchekwa kwa faịlụ site na ịgbanwuo njirimara ahụ, wee gbaa okwu alter na tebụl InnoDB niile."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using Kadupul with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4 character set as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji Kadupul nwere asụsụ ndị ọzọ na-abụghị Bekee, ọ dị mkpa iji mkpụrụedemede utf8mb4 n'ihi na ụfọdụ mkpụrụedemede na-ewe ihe karịrị otu byte."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using Kadupul with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4_unicode_ci collation type as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji Kadupul nwere asụsụ ndị ọzọ na-abụghị Bekee, ọ dị mkpa iji ụdị collation utf8mb4_unicode_ci n'ihi na ụfọdụ mkpụrụedemede na-ewe ihe karịrị otu byte."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using MariaDB 10.2.4 and above, this setting should be off if atomic writes are enabled.  Therefore, please enable atomic writes instead of the double write buffer as it will increase performance."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji MariaDB 10.2.4 na karịa, ntọala a kwesịrị ịgbanyụ ma ọ bụrụ na agbanwuola atomic writes. Ya mere, biko gbanwuo atomic writes kama double write buffer n'ihi na ọ ga-abawanye arụmọrụ."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using MariaDB 10.2.4 and above, you can use atomic writes over the doublewrite buffer to increase performance."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji MariaDB 10.2.4 na karịa, ị nwere ike iji atomic writes karịa doublewrite buffer iji bawanye arụmọrụ."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using innodb_file_per_table, it is important to set the innodb_file_format to Barracuda.  This setting will allow longer indexes important for certain Kadupul tables."
msgstr "Mgbe ị na-eji innodb_file_per_table, ọ dị mkpa ịtọ innodb_file_format na Barracuda. Ntọala a ga-enye ohere ndepụta dị ogologo dị mkpa maka ụfọdụ tebụl Kadupul."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With Remote polling capabilities, large amounts of data will be synced from the main server to the remote pollers.  Therefore, keep this value at or above 16M."
msgstr "Site na ikike polling Dị N'ebe Dị Anya, a ga-emekọrịta nnukwu data site na seva isi gaa na pollers dị n'ebe dị anya. Ya mere, debe ọnụọgụgụ a na ma ọ bụ karịa 16M."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD ọgbara ọhụrụ, inwe ọtụtụ eriri io bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD ọgbara ọhụrụ, inwe ọtụtụ eriri io ọgụgụ bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD ọgbara ọhụrụ, inwe ọtụtụ eriri io ọgụgụ bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu. Dabere na ụdị MariaDB/MySQL gị, ọnụọgụgụ a nwere ike iru 64. Mana gbalịa idobe ọnụọgụ ahụ ka ọ dị ala karịa ngụkọta eriri SMT gị na seva database."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD ọgbara ọhụrụ, inwe ọtụtụ eriri io odide bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Site na nchekwa ụdị SSD ọgbara ọhụrụ, inwe ọtụtụ eriri io odide bara uru maka ngwa nwere njirimara io dị elu. Dabere na ụdị MariaDB/MySQL gị, ọnụọgụgụ a nwere ike iru 64. Mana gbalịa idobe ọnụọgụ ahụ ka ọ dị ala karịa ngụkọta eriri SMT gị na seva database."

